15. Create Previous Month Sales Using 
DAX 
Create a new measure: 
Previous Month Sales = 
CALCULATE( 
[Total Sales], 
DATEADD(DateTable[Date], -1, MONTH) 
) 
This calculates sales for the previous month based on the current date context. 
Output 
When the visual is grouped by month, Power BI can compare current-month sales with the 
previous month’s sales. 

16. Create Sales Growth 
Create another measure: 
Sales Growth = 
[Total Sales] - [Previous Month Sales]

17. Create Sales Growth Percentage 
Create: 
Sales Growth % = 
DIVIDE( 
[Sales Growth], 
[Previous Month Sales], 
0 
) 

 
